Practical No. 18
Securing REST API as an OAuth2 Resource Server with JWT
Spring Boot 3 + Maven + H2 Database + Spring Data JPA + OAuth2 Resource Server
Objective
To configure the Spring Boot application as an OAuth2 Resource Server that validates JSON Web Tokens
(JWT) issued by an Authorization Server, so that REST endpoints succeed only when the request carries
a valid Bearer token with the required scope (read for GET, write for POST/PUT/DELETE). Notes are
stored in H2.
How it works
 Postman (client) Authorization Server (Keycloak)
 | |
 | 1. POST /token (client credentials) -------->|
 |<-------- 2. JWT access token (has scope) ----|
 | |
 | 3. GET /api/secure/data |
 | Authorization: Bearer <JWT> |
 v |
 Spring Boot Resource Server (this project) |
 | 4. fetch public keys (JWKS), then cache ---->|
 | 5. validate signature, issuer and expiry
 | 6. map "scope" claim to SCOPE_read, SCOPE_write
 v
 200 OK / 401 Unauthorized / 403 Forbidden
